shape: Tapered Directional/Twin
flex pattern: Twin Flex (symmetrical from tip to tail)
camber type: Directional Camber (rocker in nose for powder float, traditional camber for response and stability)
width options: Standard, Wide
mounting system: The Channel (compatible with most major binding brands, works best with Burton EST bindings)
laminate: 45° Carbon Highlights (tip to tail carbon layer, 45° angled fibres for fine-tuned torsional flex)
core: Super Fly II 700G Core with Dualzone EGD and Squeezebox
core wood: Stronger and lighter woods targeted in specific areas
core zones: Dualzone EGD (wood grain along heel and toe edge in two unbroken zones perpendicular to rest of core)
core sections: Squeezebox (thicker powerful sections combined with thinner flexible sections profiled throughout core)
base: Sintered WFO (extra absorbent high density sintered material infused with specially formulated wax)
balanced freeride geometry: Setback camber and stance-centred sidecut for twin-like flat-base feel with tight turns and effortless float
flex retention: Infinite Ride (overbuilt in factory then broken down via machinery for consistent performance day 1 to day 100)
tip/tail design: Pro-Tip (tip and tail taper out at points, reducing swing weight and promoting mobility)
resin: Super Sap Epoxy (bio-based resin, reduces carbon footprint by 50% over petroleum-based epoxies)
